  {COLUMNS.map((col) => (
    <KanbanColumn key={col.status} {...col} tasks={grouped[col.status]} onDrop={handleDrop} ... />
  ))}
</div>
```

On mobile (`grid-cols-1`), columns stack vertically and each becomes a horizontal-full-width section. The kanban board container already has `overflow-y-auto` for scrolling on mobile.

On desktop (`md:grid-cols-3`), columns appear side by side. Each column has its own `overflow-y-auto` for independent scrolling.

